<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Worcestershire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Worcestershire is a county in the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, with its county town at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-severn">River Severn</a>. The salt springs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/droitwich-spa">Droitwich</a> made it important from prehistoric times, and it formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> kingdom of the Hwicce, whose bishopric at Worcester was founded around 680. The Battle of Worcester of 1651 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/worcestershire.jpg" alt="Worcestershire" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Newman · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_Severn,_Central_Worcester_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3185511_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
